# Tark patches over upstream.json, applied in order by build.py patch.
branding-name-and-team.patch  # Tark name, com.gettarka.Tarka, Zynclave team
js-deps-audit.patch  # dompurify, darkreader, fast-uri: npm audit clean
services-off.patch  # no Glean, Sentry, Nimbus fetch, Remote Settings, push, Sync; Mozilla features off; no Firefox welcome
search-shodhya-only.patch  # Shodhya is the only built-in engine
mozilla-ui-off.patch  # no sign-in, Mozilla data toggles, support, privacy notice or terms rows
adblock-tark-lists.patch  # Tark list files (build.py lists) apply in Standard mode, not lowercased
adblock-cosmetic.patch  # element hiding and scriptlets with adblock-rust in the app (build.py engine)
xlit-rows.patch  # D1: transliteration rows and the one-time offer in the address bar (build.py xlit)
sources-at.patch  # I4b: @wiki, @maps and the Mac's other @ sources in the address bar
rows-suggestions-off.patch  # @ sources and language rows show with search suggestions off
look-tark.patch  # I5: Tark's name in every string, the mark on the home header and as the app icon
xlit-settings.patch  # I5: Settings → Languages: the suggestions switch, its download state, up to 3 languages
new-tab-and-menu.patch  # I5b: @ source tiles on the new tab, the mark as the menu button, no Firefox art
shield-sheet.patch  # I5b: the shield sheet says ads, on/off per site, no tracker count
tiles-first.patch  # I5c: the @ tiles come first and visited sites never replace one
menu-banner-no-alt-icons.patch  # I5c: the menu banner's mark sized and below the close button; no App Icon setting, Firefox's alternates not shipped
shield-languages.patch  # I5c: shield sheet in Hindi, Malayalam, Punjabi; other languages show Tark's English instead of Firefox's wording
signing-tark-groups.patch  # I6 prep: Tark's app group and keychain group; the debug build leaves out the entitlements Apple must approve; the release build asks for web-browser only (EU app installation later)
sync-entry-points-off.patch  # no Sync: sign-in and pairing open nothing, no Send to Device, no synced-tabs panel or Jump Back In synced tab
launch-screen-mark.patch  # the launch screen shows Tark's mark, not Firefox's logo
mozilla-fetches-off.patch  # no Monitor breach list, no Remote Settings sync for AI config or Firefox's ad-block list (the shield switch reloaded it); help and privacy links open gettarka.com
permission-prompts-tark.patch  # camera, microphone, Face ID, speech and 'Open in' prompts say Tark in every language
look-paper-colours.patch  # I5d: Nova's light, dark and private palettes on Tark's Paper colours (Android's values); no gradients; the mark on the private home page
look-one-row-bar.patch  # I5d: one row at the bottom (back, pill with a hairline, tabs, the mark); no second row, no new-tab button, no private mask badge; pill and Cancel while typing
look-pill-only.patch  # I5d: the pill is the shield and the address (share, reader view, reload go to the menu); no back button while typing
look-tile-menu.patch  # I5d: Android's tile menu (forward, bookmark, reload, share; new tab, private tab, history, downloads; bookmarks and page tools; settings); no default-browser banner; the pill keeps its margin while typing
look-menu-leftovers.patch  # I5d: disabled menu squares look disabled (Forward); no 'New menu' tip
look-tab-switcher.patch  # I5d: Tabs | Private as one centred pill (the highlight moves); the current tab framed in solid indigo, the others with a hairline
look-settings-tiles.patch  # I5d: Settings opens with the mark, 'Private by default · no sync' and tiles (Search, Ad blocking, Look, Passwords, Languages, New tab, Homepage, Clear data); the other rows stay below
look-bookmarks-empty.patch  # I5d: empty Bookmarks shows the mark, no fox, no Sign in to Sync
release-version.patch  # I6: version <Firefox base>.<Tark release> (159.1), build number set per upload by build.py archive; the TestFlight build asks for no default-browser entitlement
look-status-keyboard-splash.patch  # I5d: the status bar is solid Paper (no glass band); no gap between the pill and the keyboard; the launch mark keeps its shape
look-tab-switcher-2.patch  # I5d: Tabs | Private switch at the top, hugging its two words, Tabs first, indigo highlight that follows a swipe; cards show the page from the top with the title and × in a strip; Close all, New tab, Done in words; empty Private page centred with the mark and "How private tabs work"
look-ads-sheet.patch  # I5d: the new tab's "Tark blocks ads" sheet shows the mark, what Tark blocks and how to turn ads on for a site; no Firefox shield, tracker categories or counts
look-ai-controls.patch  # I5d: AI Controls says what AI in Tark is (Apple Intelligence, on the phone); no Firefox card, fox or links to Mozilla's pages; plain wording for the switch and statuses
translate-engine.patch  # page translation: BrowserKit's TarkTranslateCore (tark_captions' translator, SentencePiece, ONNX Runtime for iOS) built by build.py translate, linked through Common
translate-models.patch  # page translation: TarkTranslate (pinned IndicTrans2 downloads from gettarka.com, SHA-256 checked, Wi-Fi unless now, resumable, Delete; one model in memory, freed after 3 min idle or in the background)
translate-ai-controls.patch  # page translation: AI Controls gains Page translation (on by default) and On this phone (each model, size, Delete); Turn off AI features deletes the models
translate-page.patch  # page translation: Firefox's page script on Tark's engine (native endpoint, no engine web view, nothing from Mozilla), Tark's languages, Translate button in the pill, one Page translation switch
translate-first-use.patch  # page translation: first-use card (what, size, Wi-Fi unless mobile data, live progress, Not now keeps the button)
translate-bar.patch  # page translation: the bar under a translated page (Hindi → [English ▾] · Show original)
translate-faster-pivot.patch  # page translation: the page keeps many requests in flight, and Indian <-> Indian gathers them so each model swap covers a screenful
translate-default-hindi.patch  # page translation: a phone with no Indian language gets Hindi as a target, so English pages offer Translate
look-pill-minimised.patch  # the minimised address pill (while scrolling) drops the hairline border
